                                    <div class="faq-section" style="margin-top:40px;">
                                        <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
                                        <h3>What is the ideal subscription attach rate for baby products?</h3>
                                        <p>30-50% on diapers / wipes / feeding refills. Above 50% is exceptional. Below 25% means your discount / flexibility offer isn't compelling enough.</p>
                                        <h3>How much does baby product safety certification cost?</h3>
                                        <p>India BIS: ₹1-4 lakh per product. UAE ESMA: AED 5K-25K. USA CPSIA: $2K-15K. UK UKCA + CPSR: £3K-12K per product line.</p>
                                        <h3>Should I sell on FirstCry / Amazon or D2C only?</h3>
                                        <p>Marketplaces + D2C, not marketplaces only. Marketplaces drive volume; D2C drives margin, community, subscription and repeat.</p>
                                        <h3>Is halal certification worth it for baby products in UAE?</h3>
                                        <p>Yes — 60-75% of UAE baby-care buyers actively look for halal certification. Adds AED 8K-30K per formulation but opens Saudi + Malaysia + Indonesia markets too.</p>
